    {
      "title": "How Ukraine struck the Kerch bridge, a symbol of Putin’s rule",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/how-ukraine-struck-kerch-bridge-symbol-vladimir-putin-rule",
      "description": "<p>With the SpaceX satellite system faltering, Ukraine’s military launched a surprise, multi-pronged attack to take down vital bridge to Crimea</p><p>At 10pm on Monday evening a Ukrainian soldier scrawled a message on a kamikaze drone. It said simply: “The bridge is fucked.” He then added: “We will stand and Moscow will fall.” It was a freezing night, with a bright starry sky and no clouds. Lines of ice had formed on the drone’s bulky wings. Soon, it would be hurtling towards its target – about 500km to the south.</p><p>Typically the soldiers who gathered in this muddy field in central Ukraine were attacking oil refineries deep inside Russia. In recent months <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/ng-interactive/2026/aug/02/this-is-where-democracy-beats-totalitarianism-ukraines-drone-strike-force-takes-the-fight-to-russia\">the work had become almost mundane:</a> they had hit so many of them. The objective that evening, however, was unique. It was a structure personally associated with Vladimir Putin and his grandiose imperial ambitions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/how-ukraine-struck-kerch-bridge-symbol-vladimir-putin-rule\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T17:30:40"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘They were keeping it for a rainy day’: Ukraine’s Kerch bridge attack is proof Kyiv still has cards to play",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/ukraine-kerch-bridge-attack-russia-crimea-analysis",
      "description": "<p>Partial demolition of bridge linking Russia and occupied Crimea is obvious embarrassment to Putin days before meeting with Xi and Trump</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/17/europe-ukraine-russia-crimea-kerch-bridge-attack-latest-news-updates\">Europe live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Ukraine’s attack on the Kerch road bridge overnight is the culmination of weeks, and perhaps months, of military operations plus years of industrial development, during which Kyiv has developed its own cruise missiles and long-range drones.</p><p>The demolition is not quite total, because the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/ukraine-strikes-critical-damage-russia-kerch-bridge-crimea\">rail bridge is still standing</a>, one line in operation – but the attack is an obvious embarrassment to Russia two days before Vladimir <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/16/xi-jinping-donald-trump-vladimir-putin-world-peace-trilateral-says-china\">Putin is due to meet Donald Trump and Xi Jinping</a> in Shenzhen.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/ukraine-kerch-bridge-attack-russia-crimea-analysis\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T16:40:26"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zelenskyy urges allies to send air defence deliveries without delay as Russia intensifies attacks – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/17/europe-ukraine-russia-crimea-kerch-bridge-attack-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Ukraine’s president says Russia continues to attack the country with Shaheed drones, cruise missiles, and, ballistic missiles</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/17/ukraine-strikes-critical-damage-russia-kerch-bridge-crimea\">Ukraine critically damages Kerch bridge</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>French ⁠far-right leader Marine Le Pen vowed to ​repeal President Emmanuel Macron’s pension ⁠reform if she is elected ⁠next spring and ​bring ‌down the retirement ‌age to 60 ‌to 62.</strong></p><p>She also set out plans to create a fund worth €900bn ($990.54bn) to help fund ​pensions in the long term, she added. It ⁠would take a generation ​to ​build up ​the fund, ​she added.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/nov/17/europe-ukraine-russia-crimea-kerch-bridge-attack-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-17T16:40:21"
    },
